{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act criminal record screening limits","requirement":"A housing provider may not ask about, or require an application disclosing, an applicant's criminal record before making a conditional offer; after the offer it may consider only specified convictions, must make an individualized assessment, and may not require drug or alcohol tests.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider, except units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":"Applies to each applicant; after a conditional offer the provider may consider only certain convictions and must make an individualized assessment.","coverage_quotes":["“Rental dwelling unit” means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":"Dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":"Director may impose up to $1,000 (no prior violation in 5 years), up to $5,000 (one prior violation in 5 years) or up to $10,000 (two or more violations in 7 years), plus compliance orders and up to $1,000 to the applicant.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"P.L. 2021, c. 110","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not require an applicant to complete any housing application that includes any inquiries regarding an applicant’s criminal record prior to the provision of a conditional offer","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act application fee disclosure and refund","requirement":"Before accepting any application fee, a housing provider must disclose in writing whether its eligibility criteria include criminal history review and that the applicant may submit evidence of record inaccuracies, rehabilitation or mitigating factors; the director may order the fee returned.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider, except units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":"Applies when a housing provider accepts an application fee from an applicant.","coverage_quotes":["“Rental dwelling unit” means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":"Dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":"Director may require the applicant's rental application fee be returned unless housing is provided to the applicant.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"P.L. 2021, c. 110","quoted_span":"Prior to accepting any application fee, a housing provider shall disclose in writing to the applicant: (1) Whether the eligibility criteria of the housing provider include the review and consideration of criminal history","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act eviction after a successful housing provider appeal","requirement":"If a housing provider wins an appeal overturning a director's order that had placed an applicant in a unit, that outcome is grounds to evict the former applicant, who must receive at least 45 days' notice before eviction.","key_value":"45 days' notice","coverage_conditions":"Former applicants residing in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of a director's order under the act.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":"Applies only where a housing provider's successful appeal overturns the director's order that placed the applicant in the unit.","coverage_quotes":["“Rental dwelling unit” means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"P.L. 2021, c. 110","quoted_span":"shall be grounds for the housing provider to evict the former applicant if that person resides in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director's order, so long as the housing provider provides the applicant with at least 45 days' notice prior to the eviction","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.85,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","n_rules":3,"note":null}

